{"at": "2026-09-18T18:18:03.951521+00:00", "event_id": "01M2TVTSSFPVQSKNHV9DD2MPJB", "event_type": "DecisionPointOpened", "payload": {"actor_id": "cli", "actor_type": "human", "decision_point_id": "01M2TVTSSEQ2WFT93VRZ6VGVNJ", "input_key": "adr_status_representation", "mission_id": "01M2TVSPCJ6PR4N5ZMW7PYQ17N", "mission_slug": "adr-first-class-statuses-01M2TVSP", "mission_type": "software-dev", "options": ["A: status values only", "B: small status set + pointer fields", "C: coarse status + pointer fields for detail", "Other"], "origin_flow": "specify", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "phase": "SPECIFY", "question": "How should ADR lifecycle facts be represented: status values only, structured pointer fields only, or a coarse status plus pointer fields carrying the detail?", "recorded_at": "2026-09-18T18:18:03.951521Z", "run_id": "01M2TVTSSEQ2WFT93VRZ6VGVNJ", "state_entered_at": "2026-09-18T18:18:03.950980Z", "step_id": "specify.adr-status.representation"}}
{"at": "2026-09-18T18:43:00.990728+00:00", "event_id": "01M2TX8FQYA744R1BG3YWPEBFE", "event_type": "DecisionPointResolved", "payload": {"actual_participants": [], "closed_locally_while_widened": false, "closure_message": null, "decision_point_id": "01M2TVTSSEQ2WFT93VRZ6VGVNJ", "final_answer": "A: status values only. Additionally: partially_superseded MUST NOT exist \u2014 if any part of an ADR is superseded, the whole ADR is deprecated and a new ADR carries forward the surviving part (one ADR = one wholly-binding-or-wholly-dead decision). And 'approved' is retained over 'accepted' because approved carries a stated authority, which can matter.", "mission_id": "01M2TVSPCJ6PR4N5ZMW7PYQ17N", "mission_slug": "adr-first-class-statuses-01M2TVSP", "mission_type": "software-dev", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "other_answer": false, "rationale": null, "recorded_at": "2026-09-18T18:43:00.990728Z", "resolved_by": "cli", "run_id": "01M2TVTSSEQ2WFT93VRZ6VGVNJ", "state_entered_at": "2026-09-18T18:43:00.990064Z", "summary": null, "terminal_outcome": "resolved"}}
{"at": "2026-09-18T18:43:12.662636+00:00", "event_id": "01M2TX8V4P39NQRMR52DKAY006", "event_type": "DecisionPointOpened", "payload": {"actor_id": "cli", "actor_type": "human", "decision_point_id": "01M2TX8V4NQJMGZBMC2TYKYW8D", "input_key": "adr_pointer_fields", "mission_id": "01M2TVSPCJ6PR4N5ZMW7PYQ17N", "mission_slug": "adr-first-class-statuses-01M2TVSP", "mission_type": "software-dev", "options": ["A: no new fields, pointers stay in README prose", "B: superseded_by + erratum_in frontmatter fields", "C: superseded_by field only, errata stay prose", "Other"], "origin_flow": "specify", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "phase": "SPECIFY", "question": "With status-values-only settled, where do the supersession target and the erratum pointer live \u2014 non-status frontmatter fields, or prose in the ADR README index as today?", "recorded_at": "2026-09-18T18:43:12.662636Z", "run_id": "01M2TX8V4NQJMGZBMC2TYKYW8D", "state_entered_at": "2026-09-18T18:43:12.661949Z", "step_id": "specify.adr-status.pointers"}}
{"at": "2026-09-18T18:50:52.236658+00:00", "event_id": "01M2TXPVYC0QTJ1EPEDC80TND1", "event_type": "DecisionPointResolved", "payload": {"actual_participants": [], "closed_locally_while_widened": false, "closure_message": null, "decision_point_id": "01M2TX8V4NQJMGZBMC2TYKYW8D", "final_answer": "Other (Kent, better than all three offered): an append-only DECISION LOG TABLE at the bottom of each ADR. It carries unlimited additive updates without losing history, keeps current and historical context in one document, removes the hunt for changed info, and lets the ADR map change slowly and additively. This subsumes the superseded_by/erratum_in pointer fields \u2014 they are dropped. Status remains the flat enum from DM-01M2TVTS as the at-a-glance machine-readable standing. Two conditions identified in discovery: (1) the log entry MUST live in the ADR it is ABOUT \u2014 the observed failure was an erratum concerning ADR-0008 filed in ADR-0004's log, which never reached a reader of ADR-0008; (2) immutability must be explicitly refined \u2014 the DECISION is frozen, the log is append-only annotation that may not alter or contradict the frozen text. Log needs fixed columns so it stays parseable rather than drifting into free prose.", "mission_id": "01M2TVSPCJ6PR4N5ZMW7PYQ17N", "mission_slug": "adr-first-class-statuses-01M2TVSP", "mission_type": "software-dev", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "other_answer": true, "rationale": null, "recorded_at": "2026-09-18T18:50:52.236658Z", "resolved_by": "cli", "run_id": "01M2TX8V4NQJMGZBMC2TYKYW8D", "state_entered_at": "2026-09-18T18:50:52.236118Z", "summary": null, "terminal_outcome": "resolved"}}
{"at": "2026-09-18T18:56:13.217513+00:00", "event_id": "01M2TY0ND1F48V6C6N3C1EEPH7", "event_type": "DecisionPointOpened", "payload": {"actor_id": "cli", "actor_type": "human", "decision_point_id": "01M2TY0ND0EPRQN2Y3EVPBR9QD", "input_key": "adr_deprecation_trigger", "mission_id": "01M2TVSPCJ6PR4N5ZMW7PYQ17N", "mission_slug": "adr-first-class-statuses-01M2TVSP", "mission_type": "software-dev", "options": ["A: topic irrelevant only", "B: topic irrelevant OR central decision reversed", "Other"], "origin_flow": "specify", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "phase": "SPECIFY", "question": "Given the decision log supersedes the whole-ADR-deprecation rule, what triggers deprecation/supersession rather than a log entry?", "recorded_at": "2026-09-18T18:56:13.217513Z", "run_id": "01M2TY0ND0EPRQN2Y3EVPBR9QD", "state_entered_at": "2026-09-18T18:56:13.216964Z", "step_id": "specify.adr-status.deprecation-trigger"}}
{"at": "2026-09-18T18:57:40.607379+00:00", "event_id": "01M2TY3AQZ91BQNWY8XSHWD2D8", "event_type": "DecisionPointResolved", "payload": {"actual_participants": [], "closed_locally_while_widened": false, "closure_message": null, "decision_point_id": "01M2TY0ND0EPRQN2Y3EVPBR9QD", "final_answer": "Other (Kent \u2014 the question's framing was rejected). The log is HISTORY and carries NO decision-making authority, so it is never an alternative to a status change and the offered A/B dichotomy was malformed. Correct model, three separated roles: (1) a NEW ADR is the only place decisions are made or reversed; (2) STATUS carries current standing \u2014 authoritative and machine-readable, what a reader checks before acting on the body; (3) the LOG records how the standing got there, additively, with no authority to change it. A reversal therefore happens in a new ADR, the prior ADR's status becomes superseded, and its log merely RECORDS that. The hazard raised in discovery (decisions hiding in the log) is impossible by construction under this model, so no guard rule is needed for it. Corollary: ADR-0002 is NOT deprecated and needs no successor \u2014 it takes a log entry recording that Q6 was superseded by ADR-0007 on 2026-07-23, and the whole migration case raised earlier dissolves.", "mission_id": "01M2TVSPCJ6PR4N5ZMW7PYQ17N", "mission_slug": "adr-first-class-statuses-01M2TVSP", "mission_type": "software-dev", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "other_answer": true, "rationale": null, "recorded_at": "2026-09-18T18:57:40.607379Z", "resolved_by": "cli", "run_id": "01M2TY0ND0EPRQN2Y3EVPBR9QD", "state_entered_at": "2026-09-18T18:57:40.606598Z", "summary": null, "terminal_outcome": "resolved"}}
